# GitNexus index — off the PR path

The `.gitnexus/` graph is **committed** on `main` so agents have a starting index.
Refresh it the same way as app semver: **after merge**, not in the feature PR.

## On start

Cloud Agent `start` runs `node scripts/gitnexus-sync.mjs startup`. Locally, once per
substantive session:

```bash
npm run gitnexus:startup
```

That may dirty `.gitnexus/`, `AGENTS.md`, and `CLAUDE.md`. Leave those changes
unstaged. Query the graph while you work; do not commit it.

## Feature PRs

Stage task files only. Leave these out of the commit (restore them if startup
dirtied them):

- `.gitnexus/`
- GitNexus-generated hunks in `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` (`<!-- gitnexus:start -->` … `<!-- gitnexus:end -->`)

On rebase/merge conflicts in those paths, **keep `main`'s side**.

## After merge

`.github/workflows/bump-version.yml` runs `node scripts/gitnexus-sync.mjs finish --commit`
after the version bump. Manual retry: Actions → “Refresh GitNexus index”.

## Manual commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `node .gitnexus/run.cjs status` | Check freshness |
| `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze` | Rebuild index only (session-local) |
| `npm run gitnexus:startup` | Start-of-work sync (do not commit) |
| `node scripts/gitnexus-sync.mjs finish --commit` | Post-merge / CI only |
